  "metadata": {
    "family": "augur",
    "summary": "LSST Y1/Y10 Fisher forecasts: config, synthetic data, Fisher, contours",
    "tools": {
      "augur_list_examples": {
        "purpose": "List augur's shipped example forecast configs, SRD data files and parameter conventions.",
        "weight": "light"
      },
      "augur_generate_forecast_config": {
        "purpose": "Write a complete, Jinja-free augur forecast YAML (absolute paths) for an LSST Y1/Y10 forecast.",
        "weight": "light"
      },
      "augur_validate_forecast_config": {
        "purpose": "Check an augur forecast YAML for the known traps before any (possibly remote) run; returns go/no-go.",
        "weight": "light"
      },
      "augur_generate_synthetic_datavector": {
        "purpose": "Run augur.generate: fiducial theory C_ell for every tracer pair + covariance -> sacc, CSV, n(z), PNG.",
        "weight": "dispatchable"
      },
      "augur_compute_fisher": {
        "purpose": "Compute the Fisher matrix (augur.Analyze) -> fisher.csv, priors, marginalised sigmas, w0-wa FoM, derivatives.",
        "weight": "heavy"
      },
      "augur_plot_fisher_contours": {
        "purpose": "Triangle plot of Fisher ellipses (68/95% CL) for a parameter subset, overlaying several Fisher matrices.",
        "weight": "light"
      }
    },
    "conventions": {
      "kmax": "Mpc^-1 (NO h): augur converts kmax -> lmax = kmax * chi(z_mean) with CCL's h-free chi",
      "lmax": "dimensionless multipole; mutually exclusive with kmax per statistic",
      "ndens": "arcmin^-2, total over all bins of a tracer kind (split per bin by the n(z) integral)",
      "sigma_e": "per-component shape noise (SRD: 0.26); noise power = sigma_e^2 / nbar",
      "ells": "dimensionless; bands are geometric centres of log-spaced edges (SRD: 20 bands in 20..15000)",
      "step": "ABSOLUTE finite-difference step in parameter units (not relative); default 0.01",
      "fsky": "sky fraction for gaus_internal / tjpcov (LSST Y1 ~0.3, Y10 ~0.4)",
      "parameter_names": "firecrown/CCL: Omega_c Omega_b h n_s sigma8|A_s Omega_k Neff m_nu w0 wa; nuisance src{i}_delta_z src{i}_mult_bias lens{i}_bias lens{i}_delta_z lens{i}_sigma_z, global IA ia_bias alphaz z_piv",
      "fisher_units": "F_ij in (parameter units)^-2; sigma_i = sqrt((F^-1)_ii) marginalised over the rest",
      "fom": "DETF FoM = 1/sqrt(det Cov(w0,wa)); augur's get_FoM_all divides Cov by chi2.ppf(CL,2)",
      "tracer_names": "src{i} (galaxy_shear) and lens{i} (galaxy_density) - required by augur",
      "ggl_pairs": "statistics.galaxy_shearDensity_cl_e.tracer_combs are [lens_i, src_j]"
    },
    "caveats": [
      "Step sizes are absolute (passed straight to numdifftools / the 5-point stencil); the shipped SRD examples use 1e-5, which can be spline-noise dominated - 1e-2 to 1e-3 is safer for cosmology.",
      "Every gaussian_priors key must be in var_pars (or be Omega_m/S8 with the transform on) or augur raises; the shipped srd_y1/y10 examples list 30 priors for 9 varied parameters and do NOT run as is.",
      "cov_type SRD needs exactly the SRD layout (Y1: 5 source + 5 lens bins, Y10: 5 + 10), the SRD tracer-pair lists, all three statistics and 20 ell bands; anything else needs gaus_internal or tjpcov.",
      "general.ignore_scale_cuts_likelihood must stay False with a Firecrown_Factory: True silently drops all systematics from the likelihood (legacy ConstGaussian fallback).",
      "transfer_function boltzmann_camb needs cosmo.extra_parameters.camb.halofit_version; eisenstein_hu + halofit (the SRD examples) is ~5x faster per evaluation.",
      "augur mutates global pyccl spline/gsl accuracy parameters (ccl_accuracy) for the whole process.",
      "Nz_type TopHat/Gaussian are documented but not in augur's registry; use ZDist, SourceSRD2018, LensSRD2018 or ZDistFromFile.",
      "Remote runs embed the n(z) tables (and the SRD covariance, <= 6 MB) in the kernel params; the facility environment must provide augur + firecrown >= 1.14 + numdifftools.",
      "mu-Sigma modified gravity and baryonic-feedback P(k) are not generated by this tool (edit a YAML by hand after augur/examples/srd_y1_3x2_mg.yml)."
    ],
